# A deliberately small Plasma session: a second desktop for the $mod+SHIFT+D
# session switcher, and a fallback if Hyprland breaks.
#
# Explicit packages, NEVER the @kde-desktop-environment group. The group is
# what makes a stock KDE install heavy -- it drags in the whole PIM stack
# (akonadi, kmail, kontact, korganizer, kaddressbook), Discover, the games,
# browser integration and a second set of media apps, none of which this image
# wants. Installed with --skip-unavailable, so a rename upstream is reported by
# catspaw-verify rather than taking the build down.

# --- session core
plasma-desktop
plasma-workspace
plasma-workspace-wayland
kwin-wayland
kde-settings-plasma
systemsettings

# --- hardware and system integration
plasma-nm
plasma-pa
powerdevil
kscreen
bluedevil
plasma-systemmonitor
polkit-kde

# --- portal and theming, so GTK and Hyprland apps still look right
xdg-desktop-portal-kde
breeze-gtk

# --- the two utilities a desktop is genuinely unusable without
dolphin
ark

# ===========================================================================
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT: akonadi*, kmail, kontact, korganizer, kaddressbook,
# elisa, kdegames, plasma-discover, plasma-browser-integration, kate, kwrite.
# No konsole either -- kitty and ghostty are already in the image and work fine
# under Plasma.
# ===========================================================================
